  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 16,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.648,
            0.047,
            0.846,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Working with Fractions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.087,
            0.848,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. We then multiply the dividend with this reciprocal to get the quotient."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.13,
            0.566,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Summarising, to divide two fractions:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.154,
            0.547,
            0.174
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find the reciprocal of the divisor"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.179,
            0.695,
            0.199
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Multiply this by the dividend to get the quotient."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.217,
            0.219,
            0.253,
            0.238
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm { S o } ,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.403,
            0.209,
            0.6,
            0.247
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{a}{b} \\div \\frac{c}{d} = \\frac{d}{c} \\times \\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{d \\times a}{c \\times b}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.253,
            0.426,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This can be rewritten as:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.448,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.398,
            0.284,
            0.597,
            0.321
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{a}{b} \\div \\frac{c}{d} = \\frac{a}{b} \\times \\frac{d}{c} = \\frac{a \\times d}{b \\times c}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.328,
            0.848,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As with methods and formulas for addition, subtraction, and multiplication of fractions that you learnt earlier, this method and formula for division of fractions, in this general form, was first explicitly stated by Brahmagupta in his Brāhmasphuṭasiddhānta (628 CE)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.406,
            0.846,
            0.461
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, to evaluate, for example, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{2}{3} \\div \\frac{3}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " using Brahmagupta’s formula above, we write:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.47,
            0.415,
            0.509
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{2}{3} \\div \\frac{3}{5} = \\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{5}{3} = \\frac{2 \\times 5}{3 \\times 3} = \\frac{10}{9}."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.53,
            0.586,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Dividend, Divisor and the Quotient"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.561,
            0.847,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When we divide two whole numbers, say "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 \\div 3 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , we get the quotient 2. Here the quotient is less than the dividend."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.426,
            0.608,
            0.573,
            0.63
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "6 \\div 3 = 2, 2 < 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.638,
            0.577,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "But what happens when we divide 6 by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.446,
            0.676,
            0.55,
            0.711
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "6 \\div \\frac{1}{4} = 24."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.714,
            0.617,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here the quotient is greater than the dividend!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.736,
            0.543,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What happens when we divide "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 8 } \\mathrm { b y }   \\frac { 1 } { 4 }   ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.452,
            0.775,
            0.546,
            0.811
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_20.jpg",
          "content": "{ \\frac { 1 } { 8 } } \\div { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } } = { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.814,
            0.653,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here too the quotient is greater than the dividend."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.832,
            0.848,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When do you think the quotient is less than the dividend and when is it greater than the dividend?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.869,
            0.848,
            0.889
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is there a similar relationship between the divisor and the quotient?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.808,
            0.938,
            0.846,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": []
        }
      ]
    }
